    "summary": "Develop and package infrastructure projects from early concepts through feasibility and execution readiness at DBSA. The role combines sector research, bankability analysis, funding proposals and multidisciplinary coordination, helping build an investable project pipeline and improve delivery models for infrastructure priorities in South Africa and selected African markets.",
    "aboutRole": "Within DBSA’s Infrastructure Delivery Division, the specialist translates client and stakeholder needs into viable programme and project concepts. The work includes market and regulatory research, development frameworks, appraisal documents and implementation plans. Technical, legal, financial and environmental inputs are coordinated into coherent project packages, with support to transaction teams during due diligence and structuring. The mandate also emphasises product innovation, cost optimisation, quality assurance and relationships with investment divisions and external partners.",
