    "summary": "Assess sovereign and country risks supporting DBSA’s cross-border infrastructure lending and investment portfolio. The role combines macroeconomic and political analysis, country ratings, loss-given-default modelling, debt-sustainability assessment and portfolio surveillance, providing risk intelligence that informs transaction approvals, exposure limits, capital allocation and strategic investment decisions across Africa.",
    "aboutRole": "The Senior Country Risk Officer works across business transactions and programmes, supporting investment and risk teams with independent country opinions and mitigation recommendations. Responsibilities span country-risk policy and methodology, sovereign exposure monitoring, stress testing and forward-looking thematic research. The role also prepares briefings for Executive Management and Board committees, participates in relevant credit processes and maintains intelligence networks with regulators, clients and development-finance counterparts.",
